{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artificial intelligence artificial intelligence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md","fileName":"Artificial Intelligence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artificial Intelligence","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-01 15:42\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Software Engineering]] · [[Machine Learning and Neural Networks]] · [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Engineering","Machine Learning and Neural Networks","AI Futures and Human Identity","Expert System","Machine Learning","Virtual Assistant","AI Ethics","Artificial General Intelligence","aiassistants.epub","aiethics.epub","What is artificial intelligence (AI)","What is software development"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artificial intelligence artificial intelligence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md","fileName":"Artificial Intelligence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artificial Intelligence","heading":"Artificial Intelligence","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Artificial intelligence is the effort to build systems that perform tasks associated with human intelligence, such as recognizing speech, interpreting language, choosing actions, and learning from experience. The label covers both explicitly programmed methods such as an [[Expert System]] and data-driven methods such as [[Machine Learning]].\n\nIn a [[Virtual Assistant]], intelligence is distributed across specialized components rather than located in the conversational surface alone. Fluent language can make a system appear broadly intelligent even when its understanding and available actions remain narrow.\n\nAI should also be understood as part of a sociotechnical system that includes data, infrastructure, organizations, users, and people affected without directly using it. Narrow systems can have broad ethical effects when institutions rely on their classifications or predictions. This is why [[AI Ethics]] addresses present design and deployment as well as speculative [[Artificial General Intelligence]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Engineering","Machine Learning and Neural Networks","AI Futures and Human Identity","Expert System","Machine Learning","Virtual Assistant","AI Ethics","Artificial General Intelligence","aiassistants.epub","aiethics.epub","What is artificial intelligence (AI)","What is software development"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artificial intelligence artificial intelligence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artificial Intelligence.md","fileName":"Artificial Intelligence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artificial Intelligence","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[aiethics.epub]]\n\n[[What is artificial intelligence (AI)]]\n\n[[What is software development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Engineering","Machine Learning and Neural Networks","AI Futures and Human Identity","Expert System","Machine Learning","Virtual Assistant","AI Ethics","Artificial General Intelligence","aiassistants.epub","aiethics.epub","What is artificial intelligence (AI)","What is software development"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}